Runtime trust boundary and verification status
  JARs and JS execute code with application permissions, not in a sandbox. They
  load only when the application opens a trusted plugin session. This development
  work did NOT download or execute subscription-provided JARs. The controlled
  fixture source in android/tools/fixture-src is authored for this application.
  Legacy 9978/9997/5266 listeners bind only 127.0.0.1 when explicitly requested
  by an active session. Ordinary plugin initialization uses the dynamic proxy.
  Required-port conflicts fail with a specific port; optional failures are reported
  independently. Only /proxy, /?do=... and named /file routes exist. Unsupported
  /iptv is an error, not an empty success.
  /file/name maps in-memory _privateCredentials only; no arbitrary file reads.
  Cross-origin Origin requests are rejected. Legacy name-only access remains
  accessible to trusted local processes/plugins and is NOT UID security isolation.
  Different values for one name are rejected unless an explicit session is given.
  Closing a session revokes its credentials. No credential value is in this file.
  All Android device, native JNI, dynamic ART, WebView, parser and playback runtime
  tests remain NOT RUN until a device is supplied. Compilation is not playback
  verification and no claim that every external JAR works is made.
